            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xxl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Choosing the right air purifier for your home can feel overwhelming. With dozens of models claiming to remove allergens, smoke, and pollutants, how do you know which one actually works? The answer depends on your room size, specific air quality concerns, and long-term budget for filter replacements.</p><p>According to the EPA, indoor air pollutant concentrations are often 2 to 5 times higher than outdoor levels, making a quality air purifier a worthwhile investment for your family's health. Whether you're managing allergies, living with pets, or concerned about wildfire smoke, understanding what makes an effective air purifier will help you make the right choice.</p><h2>What Makes an Effective Home Air Purifier</h2><p>A truly effective air purifier combines powerful filtration with the right room capacity. CADR (Clean Air Delivery Rate) measures how much clean air a purifier produces per minute. Higher CADR numbers mean faster air cleaning for your space.</p><p>Room coverage matters as much as CADR. An air purifier rated for 300 square feet will struggle in a 600-square-foot living room. For rooms where you spend most time, aim for at least 4.8 air changes per hour (ACH) , the industry standard for adequate coverage.</p><p>Standard HEPA filters capture 99.97% of particles down to 0.3 microns, trapping dust, pollen, and pet dander.<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-performance\"> Blueair's HEPASilent™ technology</a> advances beyond standard HEPA by capturing 99.97% of airborne particles down to 0.1 microns through a combination of mechanical and electrostatic filtration. This dual approach delivers cleaner air more efficiently than traditional mechanical filtration alone.</p><h2>Key Features to Look for When Buying an Air Purifier</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KnqYBR": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
