            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h3>Filtration System Quality</h3><p>Multiple filtration stages provide comprehensive air cleaning. Pre-filters catch large particles, HEPA filters handle microscopic allergens, and activated carbon filters absorb odors, gases, and VOCs that HEPA filters cannot remove.</p><p>Quality air purifiers use deep carbon beds rather than thin sheets for superior odor removal. If you cook frequently, have pets, or live near wildfire zones, activated carbon filtration is essential for your air purifier.</p><h3>Room Size and Air Purifier Coverage</h3><p>Measure your room's square footage before shopping. Most manufacturers list coverage areas, but CADR ratings differ by particle type (smoke, dust, or pollen). For example, the<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/blue-pure-311i-max\"> Blue Pure 211i Max with 410 CADR</a> handles spaces up to 674 square feet, while the<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/mini-restful-coastal-beige\"> Mini Restful with 93 CADR</a> handles bedrooms up to 140 square feet. Use<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/the-complete-guide-to-selecting-an-air-purifier-based-on-room-size\"> Blueair's room-sizing guide</a> to match the right purifier to your space.</p><p>Air purifiers work best when positioned centrally with clear space on all sides. Corner placement or tucking units behind furniture reduces effectiveness significantly sometimes by 50% or more.</p><h3>Noise Levels and Energy Efficiency in Air Purifiers</h3><p>Air purifiers run for hours daily, so noise and energy consumption matter. Look for models with multiple fan speeds and quiet sleep modes.<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifiers\"> Blueair's air purifiers</a> are engineered for efficient quiet operation, with many models running whisper-quiet on low settings.</p><p>Many quality air purifiers use less energy than a standard light bulb. Energy Star certification indicates strict efficiency standards. Running a 50-watt air purifier 24/7 costs approximately $5-$8 monthly.</p><h3>Smart Features and Monitoring in Modern Air Purifiers</h3><p>Air quality sensors adjust fan speed automatically based on pollution levels. Mobile apps let you monitor air quality remotely and receive filter replacement reminders. Real-time displays show PM2.5 levels with color-coded indicators for at-a-glance status.</p><h2>Understanding Filter Replacement Costs for Air Purifiers</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
