        "text_Ub47yL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Purchase price tells only part of the story. According to Consumer Reports testing of air purifiers, filter costs range from $20 to more than $200 per replacement.</p><p>HEPA filters need replacement every 6 to 12 months depending on usage. Activated carbon filters require changes every 3 months, especially with pets or smokers. Calculate annual filter costs before buying your air purifier, as a cheaper unit may cost more long-term when you factor in filter replacements.</p><p>For example, Blueair's Blue Pure 211i Max uses a $45-$50 filter replaced 1-2 times yearly, while smaller models like the Mini Restful use a $29.99 filter. ComfortPure 3-in-1 models cost $66.99-$89.99 per filter replacement.</p><h2>Who Benefits Most from Investing in Air Purifiers</h2><p>Allergy and Asthma Sufferers Using Air Purifiers</p><p>HEPA filtration removes pollen, dust mites, and mold spores that trigger reactions. Running your air purifier continuously during allergy season reduces sneezing, congestion, and breathing difficulties. Learn more about<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/air-purifiers-dust-allergies\"> air purifiers for allergies and dust</a> and<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/asthma\"> asthma relief options</a>. Bedroom placement proves especially beneficial for overnight relief and<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/how-air-purifiers-improve-sleep-quality-insights-from-real-world-data\"> better sleep quality</a>.</p><p>Pet Owners and Air Purifiers</p><p>Air purifiers with strong pre-filters and activated carbon handle pet hair, dander, and odors effectively.<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/pet-odor-solutions-nontoxic-sustainable-air-care-that-s-safe-for-pets-and-your-home\"> Discover pet-safe air purification solutions</a> designed for homes with animals. Place air purifier units in rooms where pets spend most time for maximum control. Pet hair clogs filters faster, so regular replacements matter more with air purifiers in pet homes.</p><p>Urban Residents and Air Purifiers for Wildfire Smoke</p><p>City dwellers face elevated exposure to vehicle emissions and smog. Air purifiers create a clean-air sanctuary, filtering harmful particulates and gases.<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/wildfire-smoke-and-air-purifiers\"> Learn how air purifiers help during wildfire season</a> and read about<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/smoke\"> smoke removal strategies</a>. During wildfire season, air purifiers with high smoke CADR ratings and activated carbon filtration remove fine particulate matter and smoky odors most effectively.</p><h2>Common Air Purifier Mistakes to Avoid</h2><p>Buying an undersized air purifier wastes money. Always choose a model rated for your room size or larger. Placing air purifiers in corners or behind furniture blocks airflow, reducing efficiency by 50% or more.</p><p>Avoid any air purifier that produces ozone, which irritates lungs and worsens asthma. Look for \"ozone-free\" or \"zero ozone\" labels on your air purifier, especially with respiratory issues at home. Run your air purifier continuously on auto mode rather than only when you remember for consistent air quality.</p><h2>How Blueair Delivers Superior Air Cleaning with Air Purifiers</h2><p>Blueair air purifiers combine Swedish engineering with HEPASilent™ technology. HEPASilent™ uses both mechanical and electrostatic filtration, capturing particles more efficiently while operating quietly.</p><p>Blueair air purifiers capture 99.97% of airborne particles down to 0.1 microns through this advanced dual filtration. The technology is designed to deliver strong performance while running at whisper-quiet levels compared to traditional HEPA-only systems. Learn about<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/why-clean-air\"> why clean air matters</a> and explore<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-purpose\"> Blueair's commitment to your health</a>. As a Certified B Corporation, Blueair meets rigorous environmental and social performance standards.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q. How long do air purifiers last? </strong></p><p>Quality air purifiers typically last 5 to 10 years with proper maintenance. HEPA filters in air purifiers last 6 to 12 months, while activated carbon filters need replacement every 3 months. Choose reputable air purifier brands with readily available replacement filters.</p><p><strong>Q. Can air purifiers remove viruses? </strong></p><p>HEPA filters in air purifiers can capture airborne virus particles. Viruses often attach to larger droplets that HEPA filtration removes effectively. Air purifiers complement but don't replace ventilation and hygiene practices. HEPASilent™ technology captures particles down to 0.1 microns, enabling effective particle capture.</p><p><strong>Q. Where should I place my air purifier? </strong></p><p>Position your air purifier centrally with 1 to 2 feet of clearance on all sides. Avoid corners or behind furniture. For bedrooms, place your air purifier 6 to 10 feet from your bed. In living areas, position air purifiers near main seating areas.</p><p><strong>Q. Do air purifiers help with smoke odors? </strong></p><p>Air purifiers with activated carbon filters effectively remove smoke odors and particles. Look for air purifier models with substantial carbon weight, not thin sheets. Choose air purifiers with high smoke CADR ratings for cigarette or wildfire smoke. Run air purifiers continuously during smoke events.</p><p><strong>Q. How much electricity do air purifiers use? </strong></p><p>Most modern air purifiers consume 30 to 100 watts on medium speed, comparable to a light bulb. Running an air purifier 24/7, a 50-watt model costs approximately $5 to $8 monthly. Energy-efficient air purifiers use less, and Energy Star certification helps you identify the most efficient models to minimize electricity costs.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        }
